324
00:52:23.720 --> 00:52:26.430
Parithosh Jayanthi: Yeah, please go ahead, you also have roughly 5 minutes.

325
00:52:26.450 --> 00:52:29.330
Csaba: no slides, so I'll be just talking.

326
00:52:29.540 --> 00:52:37.519
Csaba: Yeah, so it's EIP8C71 LOTAS, Distributed Blob Space Construction.

327
00:52:38.250 --> 00:52:48.550
Csaba: So what we target here is, is a weak point of, of PeerDAS, which is how the construction is done in SuperNotes, and, in SuperNotes only.

328
00:52:49.570 --> 00:52:57.970
Csaba: The construction is CPU intensive, and it also scales in other VWAP count, two properties which are just not nice.

329
00:52:58.210 --> 00:52:59.820
Csaba: And then there's the other…

330
00:53:00.240 --> 00:53:10.399
Csaba: thing that the construction requires super nodes. We do have super nodes, but it's still not nice to rely on the fact that we need super nodes for this robustness.

331
00:53:10.640 --> 00:53:18.720
Csaba: So the proposal is to… Find a way to distribute the deconstruction, the construction.

332
00:53:18.960 --> 00:53:28.309
Csaba: And we would do that with, low… low topics, and use on cellular messaging and that, so partial messages.

333
00:53:29.680 --> 00:53:36.280
Csaba: What we would do is, allocate those to, nodes.

334
00:53:36.440 --> 00:53:42.090
Csaba: Just one row to each node, no need to do, large allocations.

335
00:53:42.700 --> 00:53:55.980
Csaba: And also, no custom requirements, so it would be, like, a secondary, reliability mechanism, not, not like in the original proposals of DAS where we have, column allocation.

336
00:53:56.490 --> 00:54:12.420
Csaba: And also this allocated job would be rotated, to balance the load. So, that would be a mapping permutation from job IDs to the IDs, in each slot, and, that would decide what goes where.

337
00:54:13.030 --> 00:54:15.500
Csaba: The…

338
00:54:16.240 --> 00:54:26.050
Csaba: Yeah, elements of this were coming from Full DAS from, from the P2P extension for password messages, that we're using for the,

339
00:54:26.340 --> 00:54:27.620
Csaba: On the comms.

340
00:54:28.400 --> 00:54:33.870
Csaba: And, yeah, the overall effect would be that,

341
00:54:34.010 --> 00:54:41.600
Csaba: SuperNotes, would be able to potuz on, on a single, Hello?

342
00:54:41.860 --> 00:54:43.990
Csaba: Do the reconstruction for that.

343
00:54:44.130 --> 00:54:49.379
Csaba: So we would divide, kind of, the deconstruction phase for superplanets into two phases.

344
00:54:49.730 --> 00:55:00.480
Csaba: A first phase, when they are just potuzing on their allocated low, everyone on their own allocated low, and they would share this. And then a second phase, which would be basically

345
00:55:01.080 --> 00:55:04.690
Csaba: What's happening now, which is, again,

346
00:55:05.150 --> 00:55:10.219
Csaba: Reliability mechanism, behind the distribution.

347
00:55:11.210 --> 00:55:17.949
Csaba: So that, first advantage would be that, so that, super nodes would, would do much less work in,

348
00:55:18.280 --> 00:55:22.349
Csaba: Typical conditions, which is they would just deconstruct one,

349
00:55:22.580 --> 00:55:35.550
Csaba: one, though, and you can say super nodes, could have many cores, and they could do all these things in parallel, but it's still, CPU load, so… and actually, they are not doing it all in parallel, so this would just nicely distribute the load.

350
00:55:35.880 --> 00:55:47.410
Csaba: The other part is, is non-super notes. So non-super notes could also chip in into the construction. They would collect,

351
00:55:47.470 --> 00:55:57.790
Csaba: notifications on these little topics, so the… yeah, maybe an important part that I didn't mention is that, these low columns are… we are not pushing messages on these.

352
00:55:57.790 --> 00:56:08.970
Csaba: These are just, notification-based, so Bitmap exchange, so they could collect, on, on these, allocated those, and participate in the construction.

353
00:56:08.970 --> 00:56:19.740
Csaba: Again, this would be more or less a voluntary or as a delayed mechanism in case super nodes are failing for one reason or another.

354
00:56:20.520 --> 00:56:30.520
Csaba: What this is not, this is not full DAS, so this is not, subdinal cellular sampling, the sampling is not changing, it's still coronal sampling, is the same.

355
00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:39.870
Csaba: There's also no compromised encoding, like in FUDA, so we are not changing, kind of, the column structure. This is, boilted on top, relatively small change.

356
00:56:40.330 --> 00:56:41.850
Csaba: And…

357
00:56:42.040 --> 00:56:49.959
Csaba: aims to… to use the CIP load to make the system more robust. There is also a related thing, which is

358
00:56:50.670 --> 00:56:57.839
Csaba: typical EL2 nodes looking for specific blobs. This is not helping them directly, it helps… it's…

359
00:56:58.150 --> 00:57:02.879
Csaba: helping them indirectly if they are a supernode, because they have less CPU load.

360
00:57:03.200 --> 00:57:19.250
Csaba: And I was leaving in a pod, discussing this in the IP. We can also… but I think it needs a bigger discussion, how we want to address whether we want to address that kind of inefficiency, when nodes are looking for specific blobs.

361
00:57:19.810 --> 00:57:21.459
Csaba: Yeah, that's it, mainly.

